        fp: "Defendant wished to obtain a high-end luxury sailboat moored in a private marina. Defendant approached the vessel's owner, falsely claimed that he was a licensed marine delivery captain retained by an offshore charter brokerage, and presented a forged vessel charter authorization form. Relying on Defendant's statements and believing Defendant was acting solely to deliver the yacht to an agreed charter destination for a weekend client rental, the owner signed a standard temporary vessel transfer custody receipt and handed Defendant the ignition keys and registration papers. Defendant took the helm, motored the sailboat out of the marina, sailed into international waters, and altered the hull identification numbers, intending to sell the vessel overseas. The jurisdiction adheres strictly to traditional common law property offenses.",
