        fp: "An electrical contractor was hired by a commercial landowner to excavate a deep underground conduit trench along a boundary line shared with a neighbor's parcel. The contractor brought an industrial excavator to the property line. In direct violation of local building safety codes, the contractor failed to install hydraulic trench shoring shields or batter the trench walls. The unreinforced embankment collapsed inward, removing lateral support from the neighbor's adjoining vacant, unimproved lot. The neighbor's natural soil subsided, creating a deep crevasse across the property line. In the neighbor's action against the commercial landowner, uncontradicted engineering testimony established that the neighbor's soil would have collapsed under its own weight even without any artificial pressure.",
